<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06CH">Corollary <span data-tag="06CH">9.1.3.14</span>.</a> Let $U_{0}: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{0} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $U_{1}: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{1} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be cocartesian fibrations of $\infty $-categories. If $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{0}$, $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{1}$, and $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ are filtered, then the fiber product $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{0} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{1}$ is also filtered. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollary <a data-tag="06CG" href="/tag/06CG">9.1.3.12</a> and Remark <a data-tag="05XU" href="/tag/05XU">9.1.3.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
